            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for lies down to sleep, then the Sanskrit for water for washing the feet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पन्थाः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पन्थाः — panthāḥ — \"a route; a path\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पन्थाः वनस्य मध्ये गच्छति। panthāḥ vanasya madhye gacchati. The route runs through the middle of the forest."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पन्थाः (panthāḥ) is the nominative of pathin, \"a way, a road\", whose strong stem is panthan; it comes from the same word as pātheya, \"food for the journey\"; MW gives pathin as a way, path, road or route (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
